development.solution_text:
Let $\alpha=\arccos\left(-\frac{2}{5}\right)$, so $\cos\alpha=-\frac{2}{5}$.
$0\le\alpha\le\pi$ and $\cos\alpha<0$, so $\alpha$ is in quadrant 2.
The reference triangle has adjacent $2$ and hypotenuse $5$.
$\text{opposite}=\sqrt{5^{2}-2^{2}}$
$=\sqrt{21}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.5]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.1,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.52);
\draw (C) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$2$};
\draw (B) -- (A) node[midway, above right] {$5$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, left] {$\sqrt{21}$};
\coordinate (c1) at ($(C)!0.22cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (c2) at ($(C)!0.22cm!(A)$);
\draw (c1) -- ($(c1)+(c2)-(C)$) -- (c2);
\pic[draw,"$\alpha$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=A--B--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The tangent is negative in quadrant 2.
$\tan\alpha$
$=-\frac{\sqrt{21}}{2}$

